	"notes": "The same three-column shape as MDN, reached two different ways at once: the article and the right-hand appearance rail are one CSS grid, and the contents list on the left is a separate element positioned beside it. That is worth seeing, because the screenshot cannot tell you which is which — the columns look identical and only the scan says one pair is a grid and the third column is not. The other thing to look at is the infobox: it uses `float`, the oldest layout tool on the web, and it still does exactly what it should — the paragraphs wrap around it on a desktop and it goes full width on a phone.",
